# The Vercel project's Root Directory is `socialboostapi`, but the CLI must be run from
# the repository root. Running it from `socialboostapi/` uploads that folder's *contents*
# as the project root, and the build then fails with
# "The specified Root Directory \"socialboostapi\" does not exist".
#
# Because the CLI uploads the repository root, everything below would otherwise be sent on
# every deploy even though the build never looks at it. That is what made a plain
# `vercel --prod` fail on upload size: the tree is ~2 GB, of which `ttboost/` (the Laravel
# reference backend), `detech/`, `rea/` and the Gradle caches are all irrelevant.
#
# ANCHORING IS NOT COSMETIC. Every entry here is prefixed with `/`, which in
# .vercelignore/gitignore syntax means "at the upload root only". An unanchored `app/`
# matches at ANY depth — and `socialboostapi/app/` is the Next.js App Router directory, so
# it would strip every API route from the deployment. That is precisely what happened on
# the first attempt: the build succeeded, the alias moved, and then /api/v6/orders and even
# /api/server-time returned 404, because the routes were not in the uploaded tree at all.
# Keep the leading slashes.

# --- other projects in this tree -------------------------------------------------------
/ttboost/
/detech/
/rea/
/buycodeprobackend/
/_apkwork/
/_apkwork-*/
/_refapp/
/_tools/

# --- the Android client (built with Gradle, not Vercel) --------------------------------
# `/app` is the Kotlin module. `socialboostapi/app` is NOT ignored — see the note above.
/app/
/gradle/
/gradlew
/gradlew.bat
/build/
/.gradle/
/.kotlin/
/.idea/
/local.properties

# --- git + tooling metadata ------------------------------------------------------------
/.git/
/.vercel/
/.workbuddy-ai/

# --- scratch captures and logs (root only, so nothing under socialboostapi/) -----------
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.log
/hs_err_pid*.log
/replay_pid*.log
/ui_dump.xml
